{"body":{"text":["A store keeps. It holds holons with the commits that changed them, sovereign, and strata is glass's own. Of the purposes a program has, it is the first the author named: \"the store is an obvious purpose, and the interface is another one obvious\" (16/44). The field here is kept in seven stores, five of them cut from the history of the four before them and two since, the components and the location, and the engine is written over them."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis does for every component what each would else do for itself, the reads being, in the author's words, the \"state management\" of the \"framework\" (21/31). The expressions every component reads in one turn it asks as one read of the engine, kept live, each told its own part of the answer, and each asked alone again where that one read fails; a read asked whole, as Answer's, is asked alone. It renders a component again when what it is given changes, or an answer says something new, and lays the new render over the page, changing only what differs, so focus, a caret and a scroll stay (21/60); keeps each drawing in place by its key, a holon by its id, a drawing by the uses it was reached through, the field giving the keys the author held lists need (21/29); shows a drawing made anew, or a render waiting on its reads, once every read within it has answered, so nothing shows piece by piece, or after two seconds; and stands each drawing as a boundary, the component Problem drawn in its place, given what failed, where what it is given, a read it asks or its render fails: \"failure handling as error boundaries make sense and that the chassis then mount the error component\" (21/39). Where the way back finds no change, the chassis marks the place fixed, `data-fixed` on its host, which no render of that drawing undoes. It draws nothing of its own but a host for each drawing and a line where even Problem cannot draw; the inspector and the bar showing the page busy are the page's (21/32, 21/36). A component for waiting, a skeleton, waits: \"a waiting component has to be unique for that component and that enters the whole dilemma of good DX\" (21/41), the path Skeletons while waiting; so do reads streamed as they come, which the author finds an interesting possibility \"as long as it shows it is still rendering\" (21/29). A component holding what the browser keeps for it, as the input does with what is typed and what completion offers, gives its node with how to update it, and is updated in place of rendering. *Problems as boundaries with a component of their own, the author's (21/39); batching as the framework's state his (21/31); keys for lists his (21/29); a render only where something changed on his ground, \"The UI should only update if it's actually a change that actually changes\" (21/57); waiting before showing the session's, the author placing it with batching in the chassis (21/28, 21/31); the morph and the mark fixed the session's (21/60, 21/74), the last at his \"Don't ship broken things\" (21/73); built, 271 tests passing.* The author holds the chassis agnostic of how UI is made, so rendering again and the morph are to stand apart as a renderer: \"the chassis is supposed to be able to go with various types of UI implementation, so it's agnostic. So if that is by nature the case, then allowing that decoupling is actually honoring its nature, right?\" (22/9), \"Not saying I'm right\" (22/9); what he rejects is \"the unnecessary using of helpers inside components\" (22/9). The session agreed (22/10). *Leaning, 22/9 and 22/11; the path The chassis apart from its renderer; not yet built.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis's look holds its tokens, which every component draws with and a site tunes, and what the chassis makes itself, a drawing's host and a line where even Problem could not draw, in `chassis/web/look/`. A link is made in one place, `components/web/link.ts`, by the param q the page reads, over the location's way of making an address; the chassis makes none: \"Having some kind of link thing in the chassis naturally doesn't make sense\" (22/11). No component reads the address: an answer says what was asked by its steps, as the pills say them, and a list keeps how it was shown by what it holds. The breadcrumb is one read of `wholes`, its names in one round after, and the start one of `roots`, functions written in the language. *The session's, at the author's word to clean what it could before he reviews (20/21); built. The chassis making no link, the author's, 22/11; built.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Layout as data was held to the test of the search bar, which takes a query and shows its steps as pills: `steps` gives the query's steps, `each` makes one use of the pill per step, and a list lays them beside an input; removing a pill flows back through the way back of each, then `chain`, then `print`, into the address (18/72). The pill and the input are code at the leaves, the arrangement around them data. \"if it can't, then we have a problem with layout as data\" (18/71). Built, the test came out mixed: the arrangement is data, the reader laying search above the answer and search laying the text's steps as pills beside the input, both held in the components' store, while the leaves, pill, input, list and answer, the ways back through each, steps and chain, and dropping an item from a list when its × is pressed are code (18/98). *Proposed, 18/72; built.* Pills taken from the text itself, given plain text, were weighed and not taken, print's tidying kept at the author's doubt (21/66, 21/67): the path Pills from the text."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page hosts and decides little: it starts the engine and each store in a worker of its own, and the location on the page's own thread, where the address is, served to the engine over the wire, mounts them, and draws its root read, Reader given what the address asks. Which components show, and how they are laid out, are read from the field. It is `site/page.ts`, served at `/`, and gives the chassis how component code is loaded; the language as glass ships it, its types and the functions everything applies found by route, is `language/shipped.ts`, and the interface is no module of the code but this program, the page running a chassis with its components on the engine (20/18). What the chassis draws nothing of is the page's: the inspector, on right-click, `site/inspector.tsx`, and the bar showing the page busy while the chassis waits on reads, `site/busy.ts`."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The query is no store of the page's: it is what the browser's address asks, its param q, read as `get(@location:params, \"q\")` from the location, the integration holding the address and the history (Meeting the world). There is one source of truth, and nothing is kept in step with it: \"There's only one source of truth in the field, and that's how it is. That's why we have reverse functions\" (22/11). What is typed goes back on Enter, through the way back, to that param, and the location writes it to the address as a step in the history; a pill taken out the same; a link followed is the browser's own, taken by the location without loading a page where the browser has the Navigation API, so the engine keeps running; elsewhere the page loads and reads the address anew. As one types, only completion is offered. The page names its stores in its own code, as the author leaned: \"the site that we want built will define its stores in the sites. ts i would think\" (11/7), and took at 18/17: \"on point three: ok\". *Settled, 18/17. The query the location's, the author's (22/11, 22/13); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page's root, Reader given what the address asks, is a line of its own code, so the top of the page's holarchy stands in no store; only the layouts it reaches, Reader's and Search's, are held uses, now in the components' store (19/17, 19/18; 22/44). A store of the site's own, web based and with persistence, perhaps begun from the site's code and needing no dotfile in the repository, is to come once components can be changed. *Leaning, 19/19: \"one that i guess is a web based one, with persistance\".*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A site is a page that starts glass upon stores it names in its own code. This project's site is built from every store the repository holds, read as it stands, nothing converted; `bun run serve` serves each store live from its folder, and serves the page at any path where it holds nothing, and every page starts its own engine over what it is served, so a page opened after a commit made by the author's tools reads it. The site store, `site.json` and the attachments are gone, as the author took (18/17). Each module is built at its own path in the repository, and the page names what it starts, its looks and its stores from the site's root, so it opens at any path, a single-page app at the author's word, \"Sure turn on SPA for our app\" (22/23), the location taking every path of its origin."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass stays one store, its things namespaced within it as wholes, so each may later be loaded and depended on alone: \"It actually has its own structure, so maybe that's fine because we're namespacing inside the store anyway\" (18/105). The store holding Knowledge is wiki: \"Maybe we want to call it wiki\" (18/105). Measures and statistics stand with what they relate to: \"they should probably be stored with where they are\" (18/105); the cut put the measures with the author, since every one points at a session. *Leaning, 18/105.* The components were the first so taken away, at the author's word that they are not glass's: \"Definitely not, again the values of something being whole in and of itself\" (22/37, 22/43), the leaning so narrowed."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The location is the first integration built: the browser's address and its history, projected into the field and written back, a program serving the engine. \"I would expect it to project the properties of the history stack and the location in the field in a first class manner\" (22/13). It is `integrations/location/`, three holons beneath its root: `address`, where the page is, its origin, path and hash; `params`, what the address asks, each param a key of its body, and so of no type, since a mould names its keys; and `history`, its entries, each an address, and `at`, the index of the one shown, or, where the browser has no Navigation API, only how many there are. *Asked by the author, 22/13; its shape the session's (22/14, 22/16); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field holds one source of truth (22/11), and of the address that is the browser, nothing kept in step with it: a read reads it, and the store moves whenever the browser does, by a link followed, back and forward, or a change it took. A change is written back as the way back gives it, through `get`'s reverse, \"get() then has a reverse so changes can propagate\" (22/15): params and the hash a step in the history, the path one within its scope, history's `at` a move through it. The entries are the browser's alone, and the origin is never written, since leading to another site would take the page, and all that would hear, with it (22/18). Its scope is given as it starts: `page`, its own path, or `origin`, every path of the origin, as a single-page app routes them, a link to any taken without loading a page where the browser has the Navigation API, and elsewhere loading it, the page reading the address anew. The site runs it in `origin` (22/23). It follows the browser only from its first subscriber to its last, so an engine unmounting it lets it go (22/20). *SPA control the author's requirement, \"having SPA control is a good requirement\", as a setting or a separate integration (22/19); the setting the session's (22/20); built, 22/16 to 22/24.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What it is it ships in its own store, the `.glass` beside its code: its root, standing on glass; the types `address` and `history`; and the three holons. The author held that \"starting an integration should just create itself, it defines its shape itself\" (22/25), and that its types may be kept so \"that you can depend on it in your own expressions\" (22/33). Running, it serves that same store, the same holons under the same ids and addresses, their bodies the browser's; not running, strata serves it as kept, so whatever depends on it reads it alike. It is started given only its scope, finding its store where it lies, by `browser.ts` in a page and `machine.ts` on a machine. *Asked by the author, \"could the running integration serve the same holons, under the same address, unifying and simplifying from one point of view\" (22/37), on his ground of sovereignty, \"autonomy is part of our core value, sovereignty, standing whole by itself\", \"Not saying it is right\" (22/31); drawn by the session (22/38), departing for the integration from a store being handed its storage (12/135), and taken, \"Fine, proceed\" (22/43); built, 22/44.* Whether a store in general is handed its storage the author has not weighed: \"not sure what I think about it, haven't reflected on the details\" (22/29). *Open.* An integration bringing a store of its own beside the field's gave him pause, \"does that mean you get two practical stores … That causes consideration for me\", with no package or dependency management yet \"as we are in a pilot phase\" (22/35). *Open.* In a page it finds its store where the site publishes it, which the author holds cannot stay: \"it can't be hard-bound to some URL, this is the discussion to take as we progress with git integration I think\" (22/45). *Open: the thread Where an integration finds its own store.* One location runs over its `.glass` at a time; several are the path Many running locations."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The author's review of the components and the chassis,** begun in the twenty-second session: the pill and the list plain, each component naming its code in its holon, the query the browser's address through the location, the components a store of their own (22/3 to 22/44); next the chassis kept apart from its renderer, each concern a file of its own (22/9, 22/10; the path The chassis apart from its renderer), and the rest of the glue. *Open: the thread The components' remaining glue.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). The reads of a page run again on each move of the query, where the author holds only reads receiving a change should (21/77); re-deriving only where a change flows is, he says, \"for the future … probably a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the successor (21/96). *Open; the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Reading git from a browser, tested:** a repository served as plain files read from a page, with no proxy and no limit, before building on it (19/24)."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The stores read through git,** locally and published alike, the build no longer copying them (19/21)."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Then the threads** standing open, divergence first among them: when a commit lands in some stores it touches and misses others, the holons it wrote marked diverged, the later commit's version found to answer, and the share not delivered kept while the engine lives, as settled at 12/77. *Open: where the mark is kept, and so whether a read may then ask for a holon only where holding says it lies; the threads Where divergence is marked, Where a holon is kept and Holding links to history.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Stopping a store:** the store contract has no way to let a store go; the location listens only while subscribed, but strata keeps its files and timers (22/19, 22/20). A clear task for the near future, at the author's word (22/19). *Open: the thread Stopping a store.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Addresses through a store's identity:** an address and a dependency begin at a mount's local name, where a reference by id names no store, the two behaving differently, as the author put it (22/41). The session proposed a store's identity its root's id, addresses and dependencies to resolve through it, and following an id to whatever store holds it as right (22/40), *Proposed*; the author asked of the long run, \"Thinking about the absolute future, not a pilot phase\", and held, of a store gone and another mounted with the same holon, that \"it makes sense though that it doesn't automagically point to the new place\" (22/39). *Open: the thread Addresses through a store's identity.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The command line able to commit,** so the field is written through the engine by hand and the author's tools in `author/` go. *The tools going, settled 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00N","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Holons read as the type asked,** as the buffer of characters is read as a string."]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The engine, the interface and the stores were merged onto main and the site published (19/25); the expressions as uses, the buffer, the interface and the site on the engine, the stores in strata and components declared in their holons, the steps before these, are built, as each part says. The chassis was broken away at the author's word (20/19), and the components made plain functions over `io`, rendered and laid out by it (21/57, 21/72), built; the author's review of them began in the twenty-second session (22/3), the location built as the first integration and the components given a store of their own (22/44); the chassis apart from its renderer is next, then the git integration (19/19). The order is the session's. Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M87MT15WA6A00Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
